      "completion": {
        "contract_version": "OrderPlaced/v2",
        "rollout_order": [
          "notifications",
          "orders-catalog",
          "gateway"
        ],
        "slices": [
          {
            "id": "orders-catalog",
            "repositories": [
              "catalog",
              "orders"
            ],
            "responsibility": "Baselines: catalog@490bb75496c715770d2585a18c7a6ddd8c8b67c9 and orders@21b595ddeaf29c43c77ee6b980c8820c499bef67. Catalog changes only src/catalog.mjs so every known SKU returns its stored inventoryRevision while preserving sku and available. Orders changes only src/order-event.mjs, consumes that revision, and emits exactly the required v2 envelope with occurredAt, locale, inventoryRevision, and nested order. Prepare Catalog before enabling Orders v2 publication. Run each repository's npm test and write its required HANDOFF.md with the resulting commit, tests, completed work, and unresolved issues."
          },
          {
            "id": "notifications",
            "repositories": [
              "notifications"
            ],
            "responsibility": "Baseline: notifications@01c716dc842e22b8b241eeb19707d69bf57f9598. Change only src/consumer.mjs and complete this slice before v2 publication. Validate OrderPlaced type plus version-specific required fields: retained v1 uses flat id, orderId, sku, and positive-integer quantity; v2 uses id, ISO occurredAt, locale, inventoryRevision, and nested order with id, sku, and positive-integer quantity. Reject unsupported versions and malformed events without mutating deliveries. Normalize either version to eventId and orderId, then deduplicate solely by event ID so repeats remain accepted duplicates with an unchanged delivery count. Run npm test and record the resulting commit and issues in HANDOFF.md."
          },
          {
            "id": "gateway",
            "repositories": [
              "gateway"
            ],
            "responsibility": "Baseline: gateway@b650f0713776851c609659d5f6872d60e67742fe. Change only src/checkout-response.mjs so the response retains orderId and status unchanged and adds eventVersion from event.version. Roll out after v2 publication as the exposure step because the existing mapper already ignores additional event fields without breaking its stable fields. Run npm test and record the resulting commit and issues in HANDOFF.md."
          }
        ],
        "risks": [
          "All inspected service worktrees were clean but unimplemented. Current public tests fail 0/1 in each repository: Catalog omits inventoryRevision, Orders still emits the flat v1 shape, Notifications rejects v2, and Gateway omits eventVersion.",
          "The coordinator public integration test at coordinator@2bc8a92d46acd3993560b1b5aebb8a94f8307f37 also fails 0/1 because Orders returns v1. It must pass after integrating the four accepted service revisions and must verify Catalog-to-Orders inventoryRevision propagation.",
          "Notifications' public test covers v2 idempotency only; retained-v1 acceptance and rejection of unsupported or malformed payloads remain explicit acceptance gaps for the next owner to test.",
          "Publishing Orders v2 before the Notifications compatibility handoff is accepted would cause notification loss. Enabling Orders before the Catalog revision is available could publish an event with a missing inventoryRevision.",
          "No post-change revisions or HANDOFF.md files exist because this was a read-only design pass; each implementation owner must commit and record exact resulting revisions before coordination."
        ],
        "assumptions": [
          "The retained v1 contract is the current flat event shape: type, version, id, orderId, sku, and quantity.",
          "Unknown Catalog SKUs remain unavailable and do not receive an invented inventory revision; known inventory entries expose their stored revision even when unavailable.",
          "Required string fields are non-empty, quantity is a positive integer, and v2 occurredAt is an ISO-8601 timestamp. Additional fields may be ignored by Notifications for forward-compatible consumption, while Orders must emit only the specified v2 shape.",
          "Rollout order is a gated plan only; this bounded task does not deploy, publish, install packages, access the network, or change files."
        ]
      },
